                <pb facs="0954" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2182: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-08T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1920—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 9—10:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Department’s May 4, 5 p.m. Am informed that only small band of Honduranean
                    bandits may be operating on the frontier. Am satisfied the President can arrange
                    matter with the Honduranean Minister here.</p>
                <p>The President suggested to Honduranean Minister that his Government grant general
                    amnesty to all exiles. This the Honduranean Minister is communicating to his
                    Govt.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
